=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall/profiles ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/profiles$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. ufw active on 22, hardn.yml$
# with two application profiles, not applied.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 2$
$
# Manage UFW Application Profiles ##############################$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add profile          Save a profile in hardn.yml$
   2) Remove profile       Take one out of hardn.yml$
   3) Apply profiles       Let their ports through ufw$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Add Profile ##################################################$
$
   1. Profile name$
      Such as WebServer.$
$
    > [0 or q]: WebServer$
   1. Profile name: WebServer$
$
   2. Title [0 or q]: Web Server$
$
   3. Description [0 or q]: A web server$
$
   4. Ports$
      Such as 80/tcp,443/tcp.$
$
    > [0 or q]: 80/tcp,443/tcp$
   4. Ports: 80/tcp,443/tcp$
$
   5. Interface$
      Such as tailscale0. Empty for every interface.$
$
    > [0 or q]: $
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  WebServer            80/tcp, 443/tcp$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -11,3 +11,9 @@$
           description: Lab DNS over TLS$
           ports:$
             - "8853/tcp"$
      +  - name: WebServer$
      +    title: Web Server$
      +    description: A web server$
      +    ports:$
      +      - "80/tcp"$
      +      - "443/tcp"$
$
  Add WebServer? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Save the configuration  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/hardn/hardn.yml kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Manage UFW Application Profiles ##############################$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] WebServer            80/tcp, 443/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add profile          Save a profile in hardn.yml$
   2) Remove profile       Take one out of hardn.yml$
   3) Apply profiles       Let their ports through ufw$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] WebServer            80/tcp, 443/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: firewall/profiles$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
